# SEQ-PROOF: the Sequencer on committed content - Sequences/SEQ_Proof.dseq (UE Level Sequence): an Animation track (Walk_Loop, looping) on SeqMannequin and a Camera Cut track, SeqCamA 0-2.5 s then SeqCamB 2.5-5 s; bindings name the entities by the fixed UUIDs spawned below. Scrubbed in the Sequencer (Transport.Time). Not saved.
# The level sequence ACTOR (LevelSequence component, the Play path that drives the view target) is not settable by scenario verbs: its Sequence slot is not reflected (Core/Serialize/ActorComponentSerializers.cpp:321, Details-only picker ComponentEditorRegistrations.cpp:2446), so the cut is judged in the Sequencer preview.
Проект Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/PawnNoController_Demo.desce
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано spawn Characters/Mannequin/Mannequin.skmesh 0,0,-300 --id 7710000000000000001
Дано set 7710000000000000001 Tag.Tag SeqMannequin
Дано set 7710000000000000001 Animation.UpdateAnimationInEditor true
Дано spawn Content/Meshes/Modeling/Sphere.stmesh 0,110,-50 --id 7710000000000000002
Дано set 7710000000000000002 Tag.Tag SeqCamA
Дано add-component 7710000000000000002 Camera
Дано spawn Content/Meshes/Modeling/Sphere.stmesh 250,110,-300 --id 7710000000000000003
Дано set 7710000000000000003 Tag.Tag SeqCamB
Дано add-component 7710000000000000003 Camera
Дано lua "local a = World.find('SeqCamA'); a:setPosition(vector.create(0, 110, -50)); a:setScale(vector.create(0.01, 0.01, 0.01)); local b = World.find('SeqCamB'); b:setPosition(vector.create(250, 110, -300)); b:setRotation(vector.create(0, 1.5708, 0)); b:setScale(vector.create(0.01, 0.01, 0.01))"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 400,250,250
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction -0.6,-0.2,-0.8
Дано run Open "Sequences/SEQ_Proof.dseq"
# [seq_cameracut_a] t = 0.3 s: the Camera Cut track's first section (SeqCamA) is in force.
Когда set Transport.Time 0.3
Когда 10 frames render
Тогда seq_cameracut_a the Sequencer shows SEQ_Proof with SeqMannequin's Animation row and the Camera Cuts row (SeqCamA bar 0-2.5 s, SeqCamB bar 2.5-5 s); the viewport looks THROUGH SeqCamA (mannequin from the front, 250 cm away), not from the editor camera
Тогда-вид seq_pose_a pose of SeqMannequin at 0.3 s (Walk_Loop)
# [seq_pose_keys] t = 0.97 s, half a Walk_Loop cycle (1.333 s) later: the other leg forward.
Когда set Transport.Time 0.97
Когда 10 frames render
Тогда-вид seq_pose_keys SeqMannequin mid-stride with the OTHER leg forward than in seq_pose_a
# [seq_cameracut_b] t = 3.0 s: the second cut (SeqCamB, from the mannequin's side).
Когда set Transport.Time 3.0
Когда 10 frames render
Тогда seq_cameracut_b the viewport looks through SeqCamB: the mannequin seen from its side (+X), a different angle than seq_cameracut_a
# [seq_render] UE Movie Render Queue: the Sequencer offers no render-to-frames action; this frame shows the document's command surface.
Тогда seq_render the Sequencer toolbar/menus offer a render of the sequence to an image sequence on disk
